 # Multi-View and Parallax-Based Rendering
-
-
 ## Overview
-Multi-View and Parallax-Based Rendering generates volumetric or holographic imagery by computing multiple distinct perspective views of a scene and displaying them on hardware that separates these views spatially or angularly to create a 3D effect [G]. It differs from single-view volume rendering by explicitly managing view-dependent parallax, and from full wave-optics holographic CGH calculation by typically relying on rasterized or pre-computed view extraction [S1].
-
